<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Evaluation Results</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table </span><a href="#A2.T9" title="TABLE IX ‣ Appendix B Additional Evaluation Results ‣ Is the Trigger Essential? A Feature-Based Triggerless Backdoor Attack in Vertical Federated Learning" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IX</span></a><span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> compares the performance of our proposed triggerless backdoor attack with existing backdoor attacks using triggers in a two-party VFL scenario. The results show that traditional backdoor attacks can be effectively implemented in two-party VFL. However, when combined with results from multi-party VFL scenarios, it indicates that traditional methods do not cope well with multi-party VFL. In contrast, our proposed triggerless backdoor attack is robust and effective in both two-party and multi-party VFL scenarios.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F14" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F14.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2602.20593v1/combined_impact_lr_epochs_cifar10_mASR.png" id="A2.F14.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:215/184;" width="215" height="184" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>mASR</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F14.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2602.20593v1/combined_impact_lr_epochs_cifar10_rASR.png" id="A2.F14.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:215/184;" width="215" height="184" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>rASR</figcaption>
